+# Existing Story Reconciliation
+
+**Target design specification; not implemented gameplay.**
+
+## Source and attachment precedence
+The source baseline is commit aaaec2d1ccb5856ccef9395f090653a7e2efca1f. The attachment concatenates a partial alternate hierarchy with the later complete 15-location list. Use the complete list for coverage, add the earlier planning/tracker/asset/task/review detail, and retain these explicit adaptation decisions. New design is specified, not final creative approval or implemented canon.
+
+| Proposal discrepancy | Resolved specification | Protected meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| Gate lamps replace the roster entirely | Keep the blank badge as a physical latch input | No living identity is offered; intake key still awarded |
+| Visitor Centre supplies another district key | Its named encounter uses the existing intake key to release a route overlay | No extra key item or new downstream lock |
+| Partial draft calls VC-02 Reveal the Open Route | Same purpose is included in Release the District Key; no duplicate encounter | Café lead preserved |
+| Partial café Quiet Passage/Last Order ideas | Quiet tray and hatch retained in CF-02; receipt stays optional journal material within CF-01 | Station 94 and original tape remain the reliable source |
+| All Café phrase clues become optional | Essential signal/phrase remain in CF-01; kitchen proof is optional | Chapel verification remains possible without side content |
+| Apothecary requires the lantern lesson after resin grant | AP-01 demonstrates the limitation in its test fixture; AP-02 reinforces it | No circular source prerequisite |
+| School adds a missing child | Missing place is the container socket; exactly four early pairs are verified | Thirteenth is a vessel, not a child |
+| Archive correction replaces original proof | Correction is interpretation around the existing carbon case | Existing archive item and Witness gate remain |
+| Optional carbon requires dangerous shelf traversal | Retrieval stays tethered from the raised walkway | Existing safe recovery is not silently removed |
+| Chapel survivor becomes generic | Survivor is Elian in the physical annex | Relationship and presence continuity |
+| Parish reward occurs before family-history | Expose safe first; collect contract after PH-02 prerequisites | Primary gate remains coherent |
+| Well stabilization grants core before evidence | Core is physically accessible first; owner receipt waits for both required encounters | No premature ending access |
+| Return threatens collected originals | Only a duplicate pouch is at risk; satchel originals remain secure | Committed ending and Inventory stay stable |
+| Square offers suppress-all withholding | Withhold private margins; preserve existing copies/custody departures | Witness cannot be retroactively revoked |
+| Exit optional trace replaces required acknowledgement | Brief cassette/look-back remain required; deeper ambience optional | Existing last-listen/last-look preserved |
+| Recording can be discarded | Leave a duplicate; original remains | No destructive unplanned save/inventory mutation |
+| Stay means remain forever | Stay until copies are secure, as the source specifies | No unplanned fourth ending |
+
+## Scope of publication
+Only repository documentation and its build/check tooling change. Google Drive paths in the source plan are proposed destinations. No Drive IDs are invented, no docs are uploaded, and no runtime claim changes. Future runtime implementation needs its own task execution and acceptance evidence.
